<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<!--
  Pleb's managed Openbox configuration.

  Pleb runs bare openbox with an explicit "config-file" argument pointing at
  this file, plus "sm-disable", so the session's
  window-manager behaviour is identical on every install, regardless of what
  the distribution or the user's ~/.config/openbox happens to contain. Do not
  edit the installed copy at /usr/local/share/pleb/openbox/rc.xml — it is
  overwritten by `pleb install`. Edit share/openbox/rc.xml in the checkout and
  reinstall.

  Pleb is a kiosk-ish desktop, not a general desktop environment. This profile
  is deliberately reduced to the surface Pleb needs:

    - one desktop, and no way to switch desktops (keys or scroll wheel)
    - focusNew, click-to-focus, click-to-raise
    - Alt-Tab / Alt-Shift-Tab window cycling, ending in Focus + Raise + Unshade
    - Alt-F4 close; normal decorations and title-bar controls
    - no root-window menu, no launcher keys, no screenshot keys, no dock use
    - no per-application rules

  In particular there is NO rule forcing Kilix to the 'above' layer. Kilix asks
  for _NET_WM_STATE_FULLSCREEN itself (kitty's "start-as=fullscreen"); leaving it
  on the normal layer is what lets an Alt-Tab-selected browser window raise
  above it. See the Non-goals in the Pleb README.

  ===========================================================================
  Derived from the default rc.xml shipped with Openbox 3.6.1
  (/etc/xdg/openbox/rc.xml), reduced as described above.

  Openbox is Copyright (c) 2003        Ben Jansens
                          2003         Derek Foreman
                          2003-2011    Dana Jansens
